sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R2-R4 (secrets Gateway → vault → step), env_import vault-overwrite decision, single-swamp-node. docs/reference/metrics.md#credentials.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: metrics:credentials
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 12<br/>runs Grafana
  CLI->>GW: metrics:credentials<br/>--reset
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit metrics:credentials --reset`
  %%> - syntax: `[--reset] [--json]`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - gives Grafana's `admin` user a new random password
  %%> - without `--reset`, the command only reads the stored credential; that read starts no task
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Check, keep a pending one<br/>task #5175 · vault key
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - exactly one active Gateway Node, and your Node has an access grant to it
  %%> - the `metrics` role on Node 12 is active
  %%> - no other reset or Metrics role change runs; the Gateway holds one Metrics lock
  %%> Secrets:
  %%> - creates a random pending password, or reuses the one a failed reset left; both are stored encrypted
  %%> - pushes the active and the pending password to the Swamp vault as key `metrics-credentials-operation-5175`; the inputs hold only that name (R3)
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5175 recorded with the full intent
  %%> - the active password still works; nothing has changed in Grafana yet
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-metrics-credentials
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Grafana's address on Node 12, and the vault key name
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5175
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Check the pending one<br/>Grafana GET /api/user
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - tries to log in as `admin` with the pending password
  %%> Why:
  %%> - an earlier reset may have changed it already; then there is nothing to change
  %%> How:
  %%> - official `@swamp/ssh` from 209; the passwords reach the step with `vault.get` and go through stdin
  opt pending one not yet active
    SW->>N: Change the password<br/>Grafana PUT /api/user/password
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - logs in with the active password and sets the pending one through Grafana's API
    %%> - writes the pending password to the role's protected password file, so the role's health check uses it
    %%> Gentle:
    %%> - no container restart; Grafana keeps serving
  end
  SW->>N: Confirm the new login<br/>Grafana GET /api/user
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - logs in with the pending password and expects success
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the reset only counts when Grafana accepts the new password
  alt Grafana accepts it
    N-->>SW: login ok
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the check passed; no password in the output
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Promote the pending one<br/>active password · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the pending password becomes the active one
    %%> - the vault key is overwritten with an empty value, because Swamp has no vault delete
    %%> - task #5175 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: login refused or exit ≠ 0
    %%> When:
    %%> - Grafana doesn't answer, refuses the active password, or refuses the new one
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Keep both passwords<br/>task failed · rerun reuses it
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the active password stays stored, and the pending one is kept
    %%> - task #5175 fails
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run `orbit metrics:credentials --reset` again; it reuses the pending password and checks it before any change
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5175
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
  CLI->>GW: metrics:credentials<br/>read the active one
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - after success, the CLI reads the stored credential
  %%> When:
  %%> - human output only; with `--json`, the CLI returns the task instead
  GW-->>CLI: URL, user, password<br/>Cache-Control: no-store
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - the URL `https://metrics.orbit`, the user `admin` and the active password
  %%> - the read runs nothing on a Node
